{
  "schemaVersion": 3,
  "comment": "Golden questions for the Family Archivist. 'cases' (v1): the oracle is a deterministic synthetic catalog; expectedSpec must compose to infix, and that infix must return exactly expectedPaths. 'astCases' (v2, QueryAST): modelOutput is the RAW translator text (including model quirks such as an extra 'limit'); it must decode through ArchivistQueryAST.decodeTranslatorOutput and execute through HallieTurnExecutor over the synthetic v2 fixture (catalog + GEDCOM + CyberBrain, see ArchivistGoldenAnswerTests) to the stated outcome, count, paths, and prose. 'conversationCases' (v3): ordered turns through HallieTurnExecutor.preTranslation + ConversationMemory — a turn with modelOutput is translated (the model-free step must return .translate); a turn marked local must resolve WITHOUT translation (follow-up on the last answer, elliptical refinement, local family-tree shape, or honest capability answer). Every question here is verbatim from Rick's demo to Donna (Hallie log 2026-08-17) unless noted. With NL_GOLDEN_EVAL=1 the real translator is graded by the same final-answer contract.",
